ach prestiged once... combat stat prestige bonuses +9 Attack and +4 Hitpoints\". So actual effective levels might be 79 and 74? Or display could show 70 with prestige star badges.\n\nNeed to understand. Tapping a combat skill may show detail with prestige info. Let's inspect Attack tile detail (maybe tap it). But careful: tapping may start training session (not running, queue empty). That's okay? It changes state (session). Better avoid? But navigation tests may require. Hmm, tapping a skill tile opens skill detail screen probably with \"Start\" button. That's fine.\n\nFirst, shop tests.\n\nKeep one of each toggle:\n- Toggle on, verify state visually (switch on).\n- Leave shop (back), reopen, verify persists.\n- Maybe kill app/reopen via open_app? open_app doesn't reset data, likely restarts activity? It brings foreground; may not restart process. Could press Home then open_app; state persists.\n- Toggle effect: with toggle on, selling should keep one of each item. Test on a stack (Bronze Axe x2, Iron Sword x3, Copper Ore x40). Sell action on row likely opens quantity dialog. With Keep one on, selling quantity max should leave 1. Test with sell 1 of Copper Ore? Actually \"Keep one of each item\" prevents selling the last one of a type. With Bronze Axe x2, sell row → dialog max allowed maybe 1. We can test via quantity dialog max. But selling changes inventory (data change allowed for testing, but avoid selling unique items). Selling 1 Copper Ore out of 40 is reversible-ish (can buy back) — fine.\n\n- Toggle off, verify it stays off after leave/return.\n- Maybe rotate screen with toggle state.\n\nShop header short format:\n- Check header on Buy and Sell tabs both \"2.6M\".\n- Maybe check after buying something small, still 2.6M.\n- Boundary: with 2,567,890, format \"2.6M\". Is that right? Rounding: 2,567,890/1e6 = 2.56789 → 2.6M (round to 1 decimal) correct.\n- Potential bug: the home screen shows 2.6M too (not changed but consistent).\n- Could test by selling lots to cross 3M? not feasible with inventory.\n- Could test XP Boost purchase: 2,567,890 - 1,900,000 = 667,890 → would format \"667,890\" or maybe \"668K\"? New short format for millions only, so under a million exact. That tests boundary. But spending 1.9M is a big data change; but it's a purchase and tests the shop special. Also limit one per week - can't reverse. Hmm risky for other tests? Not really; coins would drop but still enough. But QA says use preconditions; altering coins substantially might prevent other tests. Keep as later option.\n\nTrade-in capped payouts:\n- Compare sell rows to buy prices for overlapping items: Logs 7 (buy) → sell ?; Copper Ore 3 → sell ?; Tin Ore 3; Stone 6; maybe buy price \"catalogue\" could be original 10 for logs, 20 for oak. Sell prices typically 25% of base. If a bug caps at *discounted* price, rows might be capped lower than intended? But that's not obvious bug.\n- Potential planted bug: one item's payout > catalogue. E.g. Agility Cape 6 coins, catalogue? If Agility Cape buy price elsewhere is 5 coins... Hmm.\n\nMaybe better: check \"Sell Old Gear\" bulk sale outcome vs itemized payouts. E.g., bulk sale might show total different from sum, revealing payout calculation bug. \"Recent bulk sales\" record.\n\nLet's inspect Sell tab fully first. Go Sell and scroll, record all rows."}
