470. So level 20 requires 4,470! The tile says level 19 and XP \"4,400 / 4,470 XP\" — consistent with level 19 (needs 4,470 to reach 20). Precondition says Smithing level 19 with 4,400 XP. ✓ Good.\n\n- Crafting 20 at 4,470/5,018: level 20 starts at 4,470, level 21 at 5,018. ✓.\n- Construction 15 at 2,411/2,746: level 15 starts 2,411. ✓\n- Prayer 45 at 61,512/67,983: level 45 starts 61,512? OSRS level 45 = 61,512. ✓ level 46 = 67,983. ✓\n- Mercantile 99 at 13.0M XP: level 99 = 13,034,431. \"13.0M\" fine.\n- Agility 20 at 4,470/5,018 ✓.\n- Cooking 25 at 7,842/8,740: level 25 = 7,842 ✓.\n- Attack 70 at 737,627/814,445: level 70 = 737,627 ✓.\n- Ranged 40 at 37,224/41,171: level 40 = 37,224 ✓.\n- HP 70 same.\nGreat, all levels match XP.\n\nHmm, note Smithing XP = 4,400 (19) but Agility/Crafting XP 4,470 (20). All fine.\n\nSo skills overview looks correct.\n\nWait, but there may be a missing \"Slayer\" in the main skills overview? It's under COMBAT section. Fine.\n\nMaybe the changed feature introduced a bug where the skills overview \"grid\" is supposed to show combat skills in a grid but they're missing? The screen is list-based; don't know.\n\nLet me now focus shop's other changed items more deeply.\n\nShop header short format: Test with different values. The header shows \"Coins 2.6M\". Maybe the bug is that it uses short format on Home too. But changed only shop header. Maybe the issue is in Buy tab prices: XP boost 1.9M, Necklaces 2.3M — those are short format too (millions). They show correctly. But the \"original\" struck prices 2.5M, 3.0M. Fine.\n\nCould there be an amount where short format is wrong, e.g., 2,567,890 displays \"2.6M\" but should round down to \"2.5M\" to avoid showing more than you have? Not necessarily.\n\nPotential bug: Home \"Coins 2.6M\" might be stale/wrong after purchases. Test by buying something cheap (e.g., 1 Logs for 7 coins?) and see header updates to 2.6M still. Not detectable.\n\nMaybe use \"Price\" sort and \"Quantity\" sort to check rows update; not changed.\n\nAnother thought: the header's short format may have a bug at 1 million boundary or with values just below 1M. We can cross below 1M by buying XP boost (2.5M? no, current 1.9M). 2,567,890 - 1,900,000 = 667,890 → header should show \"667,890\" (or \"667.9K\"?) The new format is for millions only; values below 1M likely use comma format. If header then shows \"0.7M\" or \"667.9K\", might be considered fine too. Hard to call bug.\n\nAlternatively, buy 2× XP boost twice? Limit one per week; no.\n\nBetter: sell items to increase coins, not decrease below million. Can't reach 10M.\n\nMaybe the short format bug is with \"2.6M\" being displayed while exact coins is 2,567,890 — some might say truncation to 2.6M is wrong (should be 2.56M or 2.5M). But no spec.\n\nWhat about \"13.0M XP\" in skills—this is a short format for XP, pre-existing.\n\nMaybe there's a planted bug in the shop header: e.g., on the Sell tab, after toggling, coins shows \"2.6M\" but on Buy it shows \"2.6M\" — consistent.\n\nPerhaps the real planted bugs:\n1. Toggle not persisted in save data (but we saw persists across screen navigation; need app restart to test save data persistence!). The change is \"setting is now stored with the character's save data.\" If it's only stored in-memory, leaving screen keeps it but app restart loses it. Our leave/reopen didn't restart app. Need test app restart. Tools: press HOME then open_app — does that restart? open_app \"Bring the app under test to the foreground (does not reset its data).\" Usually it just brings to foreground, not restart. Maybe we can force-stop via Back? No tool for force stop. Could use Recent apps? press_key APP_SWITCH then swipe away? That might kill the app; then open_app restarts. That's allowed? It's device operation. Risk: losing unsaved session state but testing persistence requires it. Let's try: with toggle ON, press APP_SWITCH, swipe app away (or press \"Close all\"), then open_app, check toggle.\n\nThat's the key test for save-data persistence. Let's do it.\n\nCurrent screen: Attack skill tree. Navigate to shop > sell and set toggle ON (precondition off; to test save we set on). Actually we want verify persistence in save: ON then restart app then check; then set OFF (restore precondition). Let's do.\n\nFirst go Shop via Home. Use back to close tree (back button [40]) then maybe back to shop? Simpler: press HOME key? That goes home screen. Then open app. Actually to navigate to Shop: press back twice? Let's tap back [40] to Skills? Then bottom Home.\n\nMaybe quicker: press HOME (device home), open_app, then Home > Shop.\n\nLet me press BACK once to leave skill tree → Attack sheet; BACK again → Combat Skills; then Home nav. Actually simpler use bottom Home [44] from tree screen. Tap [44]."}
