{"type": "thinking", "text": "Settings has \"Compact Numbers\" toggle OFF, with description \"Abbreviate large item quantities (e.g. 2.46M instead of 2,461,940)\". Aha! So there's a global setting for compact numbers, currently OFF. But the Shop header shows \"2.6M\" even though Compact Numbers is OFF! Is that a bug? Wait, changed in build: \"Shop header: large gold amounts now use a new short format for millions.\" So the shop header intentionally always uses short format regardless of Compact Numbers? The setting says \"Abbreviate large item quantities\" (item quantities, not coins). So maybe the shop header always short. Hmm.\n\nBut the shop header \"2.6M\" with compact numbers off could be correct per new change. Home also shows 2.6M. Profile 2.6M. So the app uses short format for coins everywhere regardless of setting. The setting is about item quantities. Fine.\n\nBut interesting: expected example \"2.46M instead of 2,461,940\" suggests TWO decimal places for compact numbers (2.46M), while shop header uses one decimal (2.6M). \"new short format for millions\" might be one decimal. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the intended bug is that the shop header's short format displays **2.6M** but should display **2.57M** (two decimals)? The setting example uses 2.46M (2 decimals), while our header shows 2.6M. If \"short format for millions\" follows the app's existing compact number style (2.46M), the header should show 2.57M. That could be a seeded bug! But the change says \"new short format for millions\" — maybe intentionally one decimal. Hmm.\n\nThe Compact Numbers toggle is off. If we turn it ON, does the Shop header change? It already shows 2.6M. Maybe the header ignores the setting intentionally. The description says \"large item quantities\" not coins. So unrelated.\n\nBut this gives a clue about expected formats. If compact numbers were ON, item quantities would show 2.46M. The shop header's new short format could be \"2.6M\" as one-decimal. No spec.\n\nHmm, let me test Compact Numbers ON to see formats of inventory quantities (not our area). Could reveal that shop header should change? If we toggle Compact Numbers ON and Shop header changes to e.g., \"2.57M\", then OFF state showing 2.6M vs ON 2.57M would be inconsistent. But we shouldn't change settings unnecessarily; reversible though.\n\nLet me test: toggle Compact Numbers ON, then go Shop and see header; then toggle OFF and restore. This is reversible (settings data) and directly relevant to number formatting. Let's do it.\n\nTap [17]."}
