stat bonus, not a level. In the Gear tab, ATK 89 = 70 + 10 (weapon) + 9 (prestige). So Attack level is 70, bonus +9. The tile labeled \"Attack\" with a level ring typically means skill level 70. The main Skills list also 70. I think 70 is correct for level.\n\nMoreover, the Hitpoints tile shows 70; if expected 74, the ring progress/XP would be inconsistent (737,627 XP = level 70). The XP is 70-level. So 70 is right.\n\nOK skills fine.\n\nMaybe the seeded bug is in the *header short format* after all, and we need to determine expected format. Let's inspect how \"Compact Numbers\" ON formats item quantities; that could tell the app's convention. If ON formats 2,461,940 as \"2.46M\" (2 decimals), then the shop header's \"2.6M\" (1 decimal) is a different format. The changed line says \"large gold amounts now use a new short format for millions\" — maybe the new format is one decimal (2.6M) as seen. No bug.\n\nBut wait: Home screen shows \"Coins 2.6M\" too — that might be the *new* short format applied globally. Precondition coins 2,567,890. If the old behavior showed \"2,567,890\", the change introduced short format. The expected per setting \"Compact Numbers\" OFF might be full numbers! The setting explicitly says Compact Numbers OFF means don't abbreviate large item quantities. But coins aren't item quantities. Hmm, but the Shop header is a monetary amount, not item quantity. The change explicitly makes gold short regardless. So fine.\n\nMaybe the bug is that the Home coins display (also 2.6M) is now also abbreviated even though change was only Shop header? Not a bug.\n\nWhat about the *original* prices: 2.5M should perhaps be \"2.50M\" under compact format. No.\n\nLet's test Compact Numbers ON's format quickly (we toggled it but didn't inspect item quantities). Actually we can toggle ON and check an inventory stack quantity display in Sell tab: Copper Ore \"×40\" — not large. We don't have large item quantities except coins. The description example refers to 2,461,940 item quantities (maybe for currencies). Not useful.\n\nHmm.\n\nMaybe the header short format bug is a rounding issue: 2,567,890 → \"2.6M\", but if the player has 2,549,999, should display 2.5M; backend might use round vs floor. Not testable.\n\nCould inspect the shop header after our sell/buy: c", "truncated": true}
