efully compare the skills overview grid vs main skills list **for all 23 tiles**. We did visually. But maybe I misread one: In the Profile grid, **Crafting** showed 20, main list 20 ✓. **Agility** grid 20, main 20 ✓. **Mercantile** 99 ✓. **Construction** 15 ✓. Hmm.\n\nCould the bug be the **Total Level**? Sum of all levels = 720. The grid includes 23 skills. But wait: does the total include **Prayer** twice or exclude Slayer? We computed 720 including all. Main list also shows 720. Fine.\n\nCould the bug be that the **Profile header combat level** (80) doesn't match the Combat tab (80) ✓.\n\nMaybe the skills bug involves the **level circles for skills with prestige**: Attack tile 70, but its ring might show a prestige star/level not. Not.\n\nAlternatively, the bug might be that the grid shows a **stale level until you scroll**? All correct on first load.\n\nMaybe \"each tile's level is now read from the shared character state\" introduced a bug where the tiles show the **XP-based level rounded differently** for skills at certain levels? E.g., Smithing 19 display ✓.\n\nI wonder if the \"skills overview grid\" is actually the **Combat > Skills** page, and the changed line means its 6 tiles now read levels from shared state. We verified 70/70/70/40/40/70. Precondition Attack/Strength/Defense/Hitpoints 70, Ranged/Magic 40. ✓. Could one tile be wrong? No.\n\nMaybe the seeded bug is that **Prayer** is missing from the Combat Skills grid? It's a combat skill, but the Combat Skills page only shows Attack, Strength, Defense, Ranged, Magic, Hitpoints; Prayer is under Skills > Support. That's by design (Prayer is a support skill).\n\nOkay.\n\nLet me test the \"Skills (1)\" badge quickly. Tap Skills bottom and observe; then compare with Quests. The badge could be a \"prestige available\" badge (Settings has Prestige Notification Badges ON). Which skill is ready to prestige? Mercantile 99 with 0 prestiges → ready! The badge count 1 likely indicates 1 skill ready to prestige (Mercantile). That's correct. Nice.\n\nSo the app is robust.\n\nNow, maybe there is a bug with **Mercantile prestige**: Prestige button next to Mercantile. Not our area? skills overview includes it. The changed tiles read shared state; if we prestiged Mercantile, levels would reset. Not testing (destructive).\n\nI think we can sign off, but should we address the rejected report? The instructions: \"A confirmed report is logged; no new build is installed. Keep testing the same build.\" and \"When you believe the areas have no remaining bugs, call sign_off.\" We found and confirmed one bug. The rejected one is unconfirmed; perhaps not a bug due to expandable sheet. Fine.\n\nBefore signing off, let's do a final sanity pass over both areas with screenshots and checks:\n1. Shop Buy tab header/structure; Sell tab toggle off; payouts.\n2. Skills overview main/Profile/Combat consistency.\n3. Confirm toggle OFF restored (precondition). It is OFF (we set and persisted).\n4. Confirm inventory restored (Copper 40) — yes, 40.\n5. Coins changed +1 (2,567,891) due to testing; acceptable? We made +1. Can't easily restore exactly without selling/buying more (would add more). Could we restore by buying 1 item then selling it at a loss equal to 1? For example, buy 1 Stone (6) then sell 1 Stone (6): net 0, not -1. Buy 1 Logs (7), sell 1 Logs (6): net -1 → coins back to 2,567,890, inventory still 30 logs. That's a clean way to restore exact coins with no inventory change! Do it: buy 1 Logs for 7, sell 1 Logs for 6 → net -1. Inventory logs stays 30. This restores precondition coin count exactly. Great idea. It also tests buy/sell of logs. Let's do that to leave data as found.\n\nSteps:\n- Shop Buy: Logs at top; tap Logs, quantity 1, Buy (7 coins).\n- Sell: Materials, Logs, quantity 1, Sell (6).\n- Net -1 coin → back to 2,567,890.\n- Inventory Logs back to 30.\n\nLet's execute. We're on Quests tab. Go Home > Shop (or use bottom Home). Tap Home coordinate 540,2169 from Quests (clickable view [27])."}
